  "facts": [
    "The Ambassador Bridge, completed in 1929, boasted the world's longest suspended span at 1,850 feet, a record it held until the George Washington Bridge opened in 1931.",
    "Owned privately by Manuel Moroun’s Detroit International Bridge Company, the bridge carries 60‑70% of commercial truck traffic between the U.S. and Canada, supporting over 150,000 regional jobs.",
    "After a scaffold collapse in 2000 that killed worker Jamie Barker, the bridge’s safety protocols were scrutinized, leading to stricter engineering reviews and heightened worker protections."
